<title>HONG KONG: Keck Seng 1996 net rises 18 percent.</title>
<headline>Keck Seng 1996 net rises 18 percent.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-05-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended December 31</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	102.0   vs  87.0</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents) 16.5    vs  12.5</p>
<p>    Exceptional items     nil     vs  nil</p>
<p>    Net			 232.25  vs  196.80</p>
<p>    Turnover		  561.62  vs  651.35</p>
<p>    Company name	    Keck Seng Investments (Hong Kong) Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close	     June 20-26</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	July 10</p>
<p>NOTE - Keck Seng participates in property trading, rental and investment.</p>
<p>Total dividend for year is 22.5 H.K. cents (including interim dividend of six cents) vs 22.5 cents.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong newsroom (852) 2843 6368</p>
</text>
